From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:34:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 157/161] hjviewer: phones without rustdesk:// or the QR page;
 four more types in the privacy manifest

Links (C6, D-13): a pinned build takes hjviewer:// links alone.
Android's intent filter and iOS's CFBundleURLSchemes drop rustdesk://,
which upstream's RustDesk app registers too, and hjvLinkTakesScheme no
longer takes it, so a rustdesk:// link, hjv-gate ones included, does
nothing in a pinned build; a build that is not pinned keeps upstream's
links. Windows registers only hjviewer:// already (the URL protocol is the
app's name), and macOS and Linux are not built.

The QR page: the phone settings' QR button only set the server, which a
pinned build hides, so it never showed. It goes with scan_page.dart and the
plugins qr_code_scanner, zxing2 and image_picker; the lockfile loses their
15 packages and nothing else. iOS drops NSCameraUsageDescription and
NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription from Info.plist and both InfoPlist.strings,
and the Runner target's OTHER_LDFLAGS drop the pods MTBBarcodeScanner,
qr_code_scanner and image_picker_ios, which would break the link. No kept
plugin reaches the camera or the photos (file_picker builds without its
media picker, PICKER_MEDIA=false), and the remote camera view is untouched.
The Android app loses the CAMERA permission that qr_code_scanner merged in.
hjvIsAppLink and the label scanQr had no other user.

PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy adds CoarseLocation, OtherUsageData,
OtherDiagnosticData and OtherDataTypes in the form of the three before
(linked, no tracking, App Functionality), as the App Privacy answers have
them.

The tests read the manifest, Info.plist, the strings, the project and the
privacy manifest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
